From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:51:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: watchdog for lock-ups

The stall log writes a line when a stall ends, so a lock-up that never
ended (the game was then killed) left nothing in the log. A watchdog
thread now logs every 5 seconds while no event check has finished for
more than 3 seconds: what the main thread is doing (game code, checking
for events, waiting, drawing), the step in progress, when sound was
last mixed (Mix_SetPostMix), and the heap size. Only with a log.
